    "title": "Troy Police say teen shot man on Tuesday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By News staff ,\n12 hours ago Troy Police said a 17-year-old city resident shot a man early Tuesday at the Griswold Heights Apartments. (Tyler A. McNeil/Times Union) TROY — Troy Police say a teenager is responsible for a shooting that sent a 43-year-old man to the hospital on Tuesday.\nThe alleged shooter was charged with attempted murder, attempted robbery and weapons possession about nine hours after the man walked into Samaritan Hospital with a gunshot wound to his arm.\nPolice did not release the defendant’s name due to his age.\nRelated: Man shot Tuesday at Griswold Heights in Troy\nThe shooting victim told police he was near Griswold Heights apartments when he was shot early Tuesday.\nPolice said they identified the suspect after examining evidence and talking to witnesses. They said that led them to the Margaret Phalen Apartments, where they believed the suspect lived.\nA tactical team used a warrant to get inside the building, taking the teen into custody at about 2 p.m. Police said evidence technicians found a loaded handgun, ammunition and an extended magazine in the apartment.\nThe victim is expected to recover, police said.\nSign up for Times Union newsletters here\nRead the original article on timesunion.com",
